 by about 13 points in 2022. Illinois's Democratic lean, Pritzker's incumbency and vast personal resources, and a favorable polling picture all favor the incumbent. Recent surveys show him up by roughly 18 to 20 points, and every major race rater places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column.\n\nBailey has shifted tactics for the rematch, and his wife has publicly pushed back on Pritzker's attack ads, but there is little evidence of movement in the race's fundamentals. Prediction markets price Pritzker's win probability in the mid-90s, consistent with the polling and ratings consensus. An independent candidate is on the ballot but is not viewed as a significant factor.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.98, "margin": 13.88}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9753, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 13.9}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9823, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9788, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9803, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9741, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9923, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9927, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9836, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9906, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.9888, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.9873, "mar